=== T-136-base-grounding-absorbed.md
## 9. Stop conditions

Stop, change nothing further, and report (what you ran, saw and expected) when:
- a precondition of section 2 is not met, or the gate prints anything but OPEN, or a later ledger entry narrows the ratification;
- an evidence command of section 3 prints otherwise (in particular: any row with `direction_ref_id` or `term_aliases.observation_id` set, any committed data migration naming either, a live `term_relations` row);
- a red test is not red before or not green after one honest attempt;
- the sweep finds a caller you cannot repair without adding something section 4 does not name;
- a check green in the before-run is red after, other than a case asserting a refusal section 4 removes by ruling;
- `migrate_db.py --rebuild` does not reproduce the database, or the replay plan does not order your migration after every data migration;
- you would have to guess a value, a form, a locator or an owner's intent (for instance whether `contested` needs a warrant: this file keeps the refusal on every value, as `--ref-id` was; if the owner has since ruled otherwise, stop);
- a probe shows a warrant you judge to be junk accepted (O-1): record the probe and its output in the report as an open point; do not add a test of your own to refuse it.

**Open points for the owner (carried in the report, not decided here).** O-1: the direction's replacement warrant is checked for form only, and the direction is write-once; is a stronger test, or a correcting verb, wanted? O-2: dropping `term_aliases.observation_id` ends the T-074 re-judgment check; confirm that a later adjudication no longer reaches a stored form.

=== T-137-units-and-kinds-as-data.md
## 9. Stop conditions

Stop, change nothing further, and report (what you ran, saw and expected) when:
- a precondition of section 2 is not met, or the gate prints anything but OPEN, or a later ledger entry narrows the ratification;
- an evidence command of section 3 prints otherwise (in particular: a live determination exists, a stored bound is not integral, or a parameter already holds a kind quote that the new test would refuse);
- a flag name of `add-unit` clashes with `dbcore._SECRET_WORDS`;
- a red test is not red before or not green after one honest attempt;
- the sweep finds a caller you cannot repair without adding something section 4 does not name;
- a check green in the before-run is red after, other than a case asserting the digit test or a float bound;
- `migrate_db.py --rebuild` does not reproduce the database, or the replay plan does not order your migration after every data migration;
- the list of item 2's pre-build run is not empty: build no item 2 (section 4);
- a spelling is found to name units of two kinds today, or a stored answer moves under the new `load_units`;
- you would have to guess a value, a unit's factor, a locator or an owner's intent.

**Open points for the owner (carried in the report).** O-1: a kind quote whose value is written in words or as a fraction in words (`12분의 1`, `8分の１`, `viisi prosenttia`) has no deterministic reading and the adjudication gives no judged route; until the owner gives one, item 2 is not built where such figures exist. O-2: a unit whose defining statement gives its factor only in words, or only with an ambiguous numeral, has no route through `add-unit` (item 31 asks for "the exact fraction its defining standard states"); is a judged factor wanted?

=== T-138-lens-and-figure-refusals.md
## 9. Stop conditions

Stop, change nothing further, and report (what you ran, saw and expected) when:
- a precondition of section 2 is not met, or the gate prints anything but OPEN, or a later ledger entry narrows the ratification;
- an evidence command of section 3 prints otherwise (in particular: a retired figure, a live determination or a merged parameter exists, which turns a fixture-only proof into a live change to read first);
- a red test is not red before or not green after one honest attempt;
- the sweep finds a caller you cannot repair without adding something section 4 does not name (for instance a reader that would need a new status bucket this file does not name);
- a check green in the before-run is red after, other than a case asserting a behaviour section 4 changes by ruling;
- `migrate_db.py --rebuild` does not reproduce the database, or the ledger's rows change on the canonical copy (T138-10);
- the recorded output of section 3 differs (it records `add_lens_link 1`: that writer already refuses a retired figure; a 0 there means the ground moved);
- a clause is found that the `ALL` refusal leaves with no identity route and that the session judged needs one (O-2): report it, change nothing for it;
- you would have to guess a value, a code, a group or an owner's intent.

**Open points for the owner (carried in the report, not decided here).** O-1: item 2 is this author's reading of item 19 (a recorded name of that identity in the clause), withheld by the critic too; the literal reading is in section 4 with why it was not taken. If the coordinator or the owner holds the literal reading, stop before item 2. O-2: a clause below tier 4 naming no one has no identity route once `ALL` is refused (OD-47's floor exception has no tooling task). O-3: item 3 freezes the lens of every figure a live determination links, in its lens or not (`dbcore.live_determinations_linked`'s meaning), so adding a new group's link to any figure of the parameter first needs every live cell of it retired; item 21 ratified the refusal, and the owner's walkability instruction touches it.

=== T-139-amendment-record.md
## 9. Stop conditions

Stop, change nothing further, and report what you ran, saw and expected, when:
- a precondition of section 2 is not met, or the ratification entry is withdrawn as to item 55;
- the evidence command of section 3 prints otherwise;
- a red test is not red before or not green after, after one honest attempt;
- a caller cannot be repaired without adding what section 4 does not name;
- a check green in the before-run is red after;
- an amending verb changes a table whose key is two columns (other than `correct-source`'s author rows): the record cannot name the row in one cell, and the shape is a decision;
- the merge reading of section 4 item 5 is not confirmed by the coordinator before you build item 5;
- the scan of item 4 finds an overwrite path you cannot classify as an amendment or an exemption with a reason.

=== T-140-state-graph-binding.md
## 9. Stop conditions

Stop and report what you ran, saw and expected, when:
- T-134's repair is not on HEAD, or section 3 prints otherwise;
- a red test is not red before or not green after, after one honest attempt;
- the after-run loses a failure that was not a binding failure (you weakened the quote check), or adds a failure of a class section 4 does not name;
- the binder cannot bind a cited atom whose check passes today (report it; do not bind it by hand);
- a heading key is ambiguous in a file a cited atom quotes (two equal headings): the rule then needs a decision;
- a check green before is red after.

=== T-142-displayed-name-rule.md
## 9. Stop conditions

Stop and report when: a precondition is unmet; the owner has not confirmed the order against T-107; the gate prints CLOSED; the evidence command differs from section 3 (in particular, any attested form exists); a case not red before, not green after, or green under its seeded defect; a reader of `term_aliases` that cannot filter retired rows; a caller unrepairable without an unnamed addition; a check green before and red after; a rebuild that differs; a guess of a value, a body, a name or an intent; the ledger records an owner statement after 2026-11-19 on OD-72 that differs from section 4 (`grep -n -F "OD-72" references/project-standards.md | tail -3`).

=== T-143-degrees-rule.md
## 9. Stop conditions

Stop, change nothing further, and report when: step 0's datum is not in hand (the expected state on 2026-11-19); a precondition is unmet or the gate prints CLOSED; the coordinator does not confirm item 3's storage reading and item 4's warrant reading; a case is not red before, not green after one honest attempt, or survives its seeded defect; a check green before is red after; the rebuild does not reproduce the database; T-059 is merged before this task (its comparison would then need this rule wired into its own code, which this file does not describe); you would have to guess a value, a unit spelling or the owner's intent.

